<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Privacy manifest for the MemosNG app target.

  Every entry below was audited against the code that ships in this bundle, not assumed:

    NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp — PickedMedia.imported() reads
    `.contentModificationDateKey` off the copy it just made of a picked file
    (Packages/MemosFeatures/Sources/MemosFeatures/PickedMedia.swift). The copy lives in this
    app's own temporary directory, which is why the reason is C617.1 (timestamps of files inside
    the app container) and NOT DDA9.1: the timestamp is sent to the server as an upload's
    `last_modified`, and DDA9.1 forbids sending the value off-device.

    NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults — four values have to survive a launch, and each one
    is written with the API that earns a reason here. Three live in THIS app's own defaults, which
    is what CA92.1 covers: the appearance choice
    (Packages/MemosFeatures/Sources/MemosFeatures/Settings/AppSettings.swift), the library's sort
    direction (.../Settings/LibraryPreferences.swift) and the media fetch generation
    (Packages/MemosCore/Sources/MemosCore/Media/MediaFetchGeneration.swift). The fourth is the
    outbox's mobile-data choice, kept in the APP GROUP's suite so the share extension could honour
    it (Packages/MemosOutbox/Sources/MemosOutbox/UploadPreferences.swift) — that is 1C8F.1, and the
    fallback it degrades to when the group is unreachable is this app's own defaults, CA92.1 again.
    Nothing reads a value another app or the system wrote, and nothing writes one another app
    could read. Three of the four never leave the device; the fetch generation does, stamped onto
    this app's own media requests as `X-Memos-Fetch-Generation`
    (Packages/MemosFeatures/Sources/MemosFeatures/Design/MediaImageLoader.swift) so that bytes
    still in flight across a sign-out cannot be filed under the next identity — a cache-scoping
    counter, sent to the one server this app talks to and to nowhere else.

  Audited and deliberately NOT declared:
    - Disk space: nothing reads a volume-capacity resource key. OutboxRepository reads
      `.fileSizeKey`, which is a file attribute and not in the disk-space category.
    - System boot time: nothing calls `systemUptime` or `mach_absolute_time`.
    - Active keyboards: nothing calls `activeInputModes`.

  Nothing is collected: memo text and media go to the household memos-ng server the person
  running this app operates, and to nowhere else. There is no analytics SDK, no crash reporter
  and no advertising identifier, so NSPrivacyTracking is false and there are no tracking domains.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>C617.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>CA92.1</string>
                <string>1C8F.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
